ionedConcurrency.requestedConcurrency.description.html":"To enable your function to scale without fluctuations in latency, use provisioned concurrency. You can use Application Auto Scaling to automatically adjust provisioned concurrency to maintain a configured target utilization. Provisioned concurrency runs continually and has separate pricing for concurrency and execution duration. <learn-more> </learn-more>","editProvisionedConcurrency.requestedConcurrency.constraintText":"{provisionedConcurrencyLimit} available","editProvisionedConcurrency.sentRequest.successful":"Created provisioned concurrency configuration. Allocating provisioned concurrency can take a few minutes.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyVersion.errorText.setOnAlias":"The version already has provisioned concurrency from an alias ({aliasName}).","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyVersion.errorText.latest":"Can't provision concurrency for $LATEST. Choose a published version or alias.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyVersion.errorText.alreadyCreated":"The version already has provisioned concurrency.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyAlias.errorText.setOnVersion":"The alias's version is targeted by another provisioned concurrency configuration.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyAlias.errorText.setOnLatestVersion":"You can't allocate provisioned concurrency for an alias that points to $LATEST. Choose an alias that points to a function version.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyAlias.errorText.weightedAlias":"The alias is weighted between two versions. Configure provisioned concurrency on an alias before adding a routing configuration.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyAlias.errorText.weightedAlias.edit":"Can't modify provisioned concurrency for a weighted alias.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrencyAlias.errorText.alreadyCreated":"The alias is already configured with provisioned concurrency.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrency.errorText.aboveReserved":"The maximum allowed provisioned concurrency is {provisionedConcurrencyLimit}, based on the function's reserved concurrency ({reservedConcurrency}) minus the provisioned concurrency on other versions ({provisionedConcurrency}).","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrency.errorText.aboveUnreserved":"The maximum allowed provisioned concurrency is {provisionedConcurrencyLimit}, based on the unreserved concurrency available ({unreservedConcurrency}) minus the minimum unreserved account concurrency ({unreservedConcurrencyMinimum}).","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrency.errorText.lowerOrEqualToZero":"The minimum provisioned concurrency value allowed is 1.","editProvisionedConcurrency.provisionedConcurrency.errorText.noDecimal":"The value must be a positive whole number.","recursionConfig.description":"Recursive loop detection automatically detects and stops infinite recursive loops involving your functions and supported AWS services. This feature is free for all customers.","recursionConfig.header":"Recursive loop detection","recursionConfig.recursiveLoop":"Recursion detection configuration","recursionConfig.warning":"Your function is not currently protected from being invoked in an infinite recursive loop. Edit your function's configuration to protect against unexpected charges being billed to your AWS account.","editRecursionConfig.header":"Edit recursive loop detection","editRecursionConfig.Allow":"Allow recursive loops","editRecursionConfig.Terminate":"Terminate recursive loops","editRecursionConfig.field.label":"Recursion detection configuration","editRecursionConfig.Allow.description":"Lambda takes no action when it detects recursive loops.","editRecursionConfig.Terminate.description":"Lambda stops your function being invoked and notifies you when it detects a recursive loop.","editRecursionConfig.blurb":"Lambda currently detects only recursive loops involving Lambda, Amazon SQS, and Amazon SNS.","editRecursionConfig.warning":"Your function won't be protected from being invoked in an infinite recursive loop. Use caution and implement suitable guard rails to prevent unexpected charges being billed to your AWS account.","display.version":"version:{version}","display.weightedAlias":"version:{version1} (weight: {weight1}%), version:{version2} (weight: {weight2}%)","display.weightedAliasInProgress":"version:{version1}, version:{version2}","display.versionWithWeight":"version:{versionName}, weight: {weight}%, description: {description}","role.tooltip":"Choose a role that defines the permissions of your function. To create a custom role, go to the <link>IAM console</link>.","role.existing.label":"Existing role","role.existing.subtext":"<link>View the {roleName} role</link> on the IAM console.","role.template.label":"Policy templates","search.general.placeholderSearch":"Search by keyword","add.button.submit":"Add","createFunction.existingRole.field.description":"Choose an existing role that you've created to be used with this Lambda function. The role must have permission to upload logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","executionRole.existingRole.field.description":"Choose an existing role that you've created to be used with this Lambda function. The role must have permission to upload logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","configureBlueprint.existingRole.field.description":"Choose an existing role that you've created to be used with this Lambda function. The role must have permission to upload logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","functionDesigner.tab.permissions.resourcePolicy.title":"Resource-based policy","functionDesigner.tab.permissions.resourcePolicy.viewJson":"View policy","functionDesigner.tab.permissions.resourcePolicy.json.header":"Resource-based policy document","functionDesigner.tab.permissions.resourcePolicy.description":"Resource-based policies grant other AWS accounts and services permissions to access your Lambda resources.","edit.saveSuccess":"Your changes have been saved.","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.title":"Logging configuration","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.edit":"Edit","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.cloudWatch.label":"CloudWatch log group","functionDetail.sections.additionalMonitoringTools.title":"Additional monitoring tools","functionDetail.sections.additionalMonitoringTools.edit":"Edit","functionDetail.sections.additionalMonitoringTools.xray.label":"X-Ray active tracing","functionDetail.sections.additionalMonitoringTools.codeGuru.label":"CodeGuru code profiling","functionDetail.sections.loggingContent.title":"Log content","functionDetail.sections.loggingDestination.title":"Log destination","editLoggingConfiguration.header":"Edit logging configuration","editLoggingConfiguration.title":"Edit logging configuration","editLoggingConfiguration.loggingConfiguration.title.readonly":"Logging configuration","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customLogGroup.label":"Custom log group","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogGroup.label":"Log group","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.label":"CloudWatch log group","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.description":"By default, CloudWatch automatically creates a log group for your Lambda function when it's first invoked. To use an existing log group, or to manually create a new one for your function to use, choose Custom.","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.defaultText":"Default (<link>/aws/lambda/{functionName}</link>)","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customText":"Custom","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customLogGroup.placeholder":"Custom log group","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customLogGroup.description":"To create a new log group, enter a new name. Log group names must be unique within a Region for an AWS account. To choose an existing CloudWatch log group, enter its name. For cross-account log delivery, enter a log group associated with a <link>cross-account subscription filter</link>.","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customLogGroup.alert.text":'The <b>"{logGroup}"</b> is not the current log group for this function. If this log group doesn\'t exist, Lambda will create it when your function is first invoked. If a log group named "{logGroup}" already exists, Lambda will start sending logs for this function to that group.',"functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.applicationLogLevel.label":"Application log level","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.systemLogLevel.label":"System log level","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.logFormat.label":"Log format","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.logGroup.label":"CloudWatch log group","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.loggingContent.label":"Log content","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.loggingDestination.label":"Log destination","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.logDestinationArn.label":"Log destination","functionDetail.sections.loggingConfiguration.logDestinationIamRole.label":"CloudWatch IAM role","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.customLogGroup.hint":"Valid characters: <b>a-z</b>, <b>A-Z</b>, <b>0-9</b>, <b>_</b> (underscore), <b>-</b> (hyphen), <b>/</b> (forward slash), <b>.</b> (period), and <b>#</b> (number sign). Log group names cannot exceed 512 characters.","editLoggingConfiguration.content":"Log content","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.label":"Log format","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.description":"For more control and better readability, we recommend choosing JSON for your log format. You can customize your function's logging level only for JSON.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.Text":"Text","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.JSON":"JSON","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.disabledReason":"Text log format isn't supported for functions with capacity provider compute.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogFormat.disabledReasonDurable":"Text log format isn't supported for durable function.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.label":"Destination service","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.description":"Choose a destination to store and analyze your logs. You can send your logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon S3, or Amazon Data Firehose.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.cloudWatchLogs.label":"Amazon CloudWatch Logs","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.cloudWatchLogs.description":"Use Logs Insights to analyze logs. Create metrics and alarms.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.s3.label":"Amazon S3","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.s3.description":"Store logs for long-term archiving.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.fireHose.label":"Amazon Data Firehose","editLoggingConfiguration.selectLogDestination.fireHose.description":"Stream logs in real time to OpenSearch Service, Redshift, or other applications and endpoints.","editLoggingConfiguration.deliveryLogGroup.label":"CloudWatch delivery log group","editLoggingConfiguration.deliveryLogGroup.description":"Log delivery to Amazon S3 or Amazon Data Firehose requires using a log group with delivery log class. This log class enables efficient routing but doesn't support standard CloudWatch Logs features such as Logs Insights and Live Tail.","editLoggingConfiguration.deliveryLogGroup.create.label":"Log group name","editLoggingConfiguration.deliveryLogGroup.placeholder":"Enter log group name","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.create.label":"Create new log group","editLoggingConfiguration.cloudWatchLog.exist.label":"Existing log group","editLoggingConfiguration.s3.nonCompatible.alert.text":"Logs will go to S3 if you save. Although you selected Firehose, this log group is configured for S3. To send logs to Firehose, either choose a log group configured for Firehose or create a new delivery log group before saving.","editLoggingConfiguration.fireHose.nonCompatible.alert.text":"Logs will go to Firehose if you save. Although you selected S3, this log group is configured for Firehose. To send logs to S3, either choose a log group configured for S3 or create a new delivery log group before saving.","editLoggingConfiguration.noDestination.alert.text":"Lambda will not send logs to any destination if you save. This log group doesn't have a configured destination. To enable logging, either select a log group with a configured destination or create a new delivery log group before saving.","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.s3.label":"Destination S3 Bucket","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.s3.description":"Choose a bucket or enter its ARN. Logs can only be delivered to a single S3 bucket. The bucket must be in the same account and same Region as the function.","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.s3.placeholder":"Choose or enter S3 Bucket ARN","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.fireHose.label":"Amazon Data Firehose Stream","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.fireHose.description":"Choose a delivery stream or enter its ARN. This supports same-account and cross-account delivery streams in the same Region. <link>Create a new Data Firehose</link>","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.fireHose.placeholder":"Choose or enter Data Firehose ARN","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.iamRole.label":"IAM role for CloudWatch delivery log group","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.iamRole.description":"Grant permission for CloudWatch Logs to deliver logs to S3 or Firehose.  <link>Create a new IAM role</link>","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.iamRole.placeholder":"Choose or enter IAM role ARN","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.deliveryLogGroup.label":"Delivery log group","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.deliveryLogGroup.description":"A delivery log group can only support one destination at a time.","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.notSupported":"Not supported","editLoggingConfiguration.logDestination.none":"None","editLoggingConfiguration.selectAppLevel.label":"Application log level","editLoggingConfiguration.selectAppLevel.description":"Application logs are the logs that your function code generates, also known as function logs. Choosing a more detailed logging level can incur additional costs from CloudWatch Logs.","editLoggingConfiguration.selectSysLevel.label":"System log level","editLoggingConfiguration.selectSysLevel.description":"System logs are the logs that Lambda generates, also known as platform logs. Choosing a more detailed logging level can incur additional costs from CloudWatch Logs.","permissions.editLoggingConfiguration.header.description":"If your function’s execution role doesn’t have permission to upload logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Lambda will add this permission to the role.","permissions.editLoggingConfiguration.body.description":"For more information about required permissions, see the {externalLink} documentation.","permissions.editLoggingConfiguration.body.description.loggingConfiguration":"Lambda logging Configuration","editMonitoringTools.tracer.field.label":"X-Ray active tracing","editMonitoringTools.tracer.field.key":"X-Ray active tracing","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsights.field.label":"Lambda Insights enhanced monitoring","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsights.field.key":"Lambda Insights enhanced monitoring","editMonitoringTools.sections.tracer.title":"AWS X-Ray","editMonitoringTools.header":"Edit monitoring tools","editMonitoringTools.monitoring.xray.warning":"Your function's execution role doesn't have permissions to send trace data to AWS X-Ray. Lambda will try to add the required permissions to the role.","editMonitoringTools.sections.cloudwatch.title":"Amazon CloudWatch","editMonitoringTools.cloudwatch.field.label":"Logs and metrics (default)","editMonitoringTools.cloudwatch.field.key":"CloudWatch logs","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.status.disabled":"Not enabled","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.status.success":"Enabled","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.status.warning":"Warning - need permission","editMonitoringTools.cloudwatchFooter.warning.role":"Your execution role doesn't have permission to send logs to CloudWatch. You can add CloudWatch Logs permissions using the AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole AWS managed policy provided by Lambda.","editMonitoringTools.cloudwatch.description":"By default, Lambda functions produce a CloudWatch Logs stream and standard metrics.","editMonitoringTools.tracer.description":"AWS X-Ray collects data about events that your function processes to help identify performance bottlenecks and troubleshoot issues. If your execution role doesn't have the required permissions for X-Ray, Lambda attempts to add them to the role. After turning on active tracing, use the {page} to instrument your Lambda function.","editMonitoringTools.tracer.description.page":"X-Ray SDK","editMonitoringTools.sections.lambdaInsights.title":"CloudWatch Lambda Insights","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsights.description":"Turn on to collect system-level metrics including CPU time, memory, disk, and network usage.","editMonitoringTools.xRayFooter.warning.role":"Couldn't find the required permissions. The Lambda console will attempt to add them to the execution role. Be sure that your execution role does not deny the required permissions.","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsightsFooter.warning.role":"Couldn't find the required permissions. The Lambda console will attempt to add them to the execution role. Be sure that your execution role does not deny the required permissions.","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsightsFooter.toggle.description.disabled":"Your function runtime is not yet supported by Lambda Insights. You must switch to a compatible runtime.","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsightsFooter.warning.arm.header":"Your function's arm64 architecture doesn't support CloudWatch Lambda Insights","editMonitoringTools.lambdaInsightsFooter.warning.arm.description":"Function execution will fail until you turn off <b>CloudWatch Lambda Insights</b> for your function.","editMonitoringTools.sections.codeGuru.title":"Amazon CodeGuru Profiler","editMonitoringTools.codeGuru.description.page":"Using CodeGuru Profiler with your Lambda function","editMonitoringTools.codeGuru.description":"Turn on to collect performance data and to see recommendations for optimizing your application. When you turn on CodeGuru Profiler, Lambda adds environment variables to your function. Visit {page} to learn more.","editMonitoringTools.codeGuruFooter.warning":"Couldn't find the required permissions or environment variables. The Lambda console will attempt to add them. Be sure that your execution role does not deny the required permissions.","editMonitoringTools.codeGuruFooter.toggle.description.disabled":"You cannot activate CodeGuru Profiler from the console with your function’s current runtime. To turn on code profiling, change to a compatible runtime.","editMonitoringTools.codeGuru.field.label":"CodeGuru code profiling","editMonitoringTools.codeGuru.field.key":"CodeGuru code profiling","editMonitoringTools.configuration.enable":"Enabled","editMonitoringTools.configuration.notEnabled":"Not enabled","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.field.title.label":"CloudWatch Application Signals and AWS X-Ray","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.field.label":"Application Signals","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.slr.alert.header":"Actions required for discovery","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.slr.alert.body":"Application Signals needs permission to discover your function's metrics and traces. You need to do this only once for your account.","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.slr.alert.action":"Start discovery","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.alert.header":"Environment variable conflict","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.alert.body":"Application Signals requires that you set the <environmentVariableKey> </environmentVariableKey> environment variable to a specific value. Currently, your function's <environmentVariableKey> </environmentVariableKey> environment variable is assigned another value.","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.warning.currentValue":"Current value: <currentExecWrapperValue> </currentExecWrapperValue>","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.warning.targetValue":"Required value: <newExecWrapperValue> </newExecWrapperValue>","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.alert.body.cta":"You can choose to override to the required value automatically using the checkbox below, or manually update the value.","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.envVar.autoSet.label":"Override environment variable for Application Signals","editMonitoringTools.tracing.field.label":"Lambda service traces","editMonitoringTools.sections.appSignalXRay.description":"CloudWatch Application Signals and AWS X-Ray help you monitor the performance and health of your application.","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.field.subtitle.label":"Application Signals","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.field.description":"Application Signals helps you collect application traces and metrics such as requests, availability, latency, errors, and faults. You can view these traces and metrics in the <link>CloudWatch console</link>.","editMonitoringTools.tracing.field.description":"Lambda service X-Ray traces help you track the path of a request through your application. You can view these traces in the <link>X-Ray console</link>.","editMonitoringTools.appSignal.field.hint":"Supported runtimes: {runtimes}. (Current runtime: {currentRuntime})","editMonitoringTools.monitoringToolConflict.alert.header":"Monitoring service conflict","editMonitoringTools.monitoringToolConflict.alert.description":"{disabledService} cannot be enabled simultaneously with {enabledService}. To enable one, you must disable the other.","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.appSignalLatencyInfo":"Application Signals can take up to 10 minutes to discover your function after your updated function is invoked. After Application Signals discovers your function, you can visualize its metrics and traces in the CloudWatch console.","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.permissions.header":"Potential missing permissions","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.permissions.description":"The IAM Policy Simulator indicates that your function's execution role may be missing permissions to integrate with {serviceName}. The policy simulator results can differ from your live AWS environment. <link>Learn more about required permissions</link>","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.slr.header":"Actions required for discovery","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.slr.description":"Application Signals needs permission to discover your function's metrics and traces. You need to do this only once for your account. <link>Start discovery</link>","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.envVar.header":"Misconfigured environment variable","functionDetail.sections.monitoringTools.warningStatus.envVar.description":"You enabled {serviceName}, but the <envVarName> </envVarName> environment variable is misconfigured. <link>Learn more about this environment variable</link>","editBasicSettings.existingRole.field.description":"Choose an existing role that you've created to be used with this Lambda function. The role must have permission to upload logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","editRelation.header":"Edit trigger","create.error.validation.func":"Correct the errors above and try again.","functionDetail.flashBar.updateSuccess":"Successfully updated the function <b>{functionName}</b>.","functionDetail.button.createAlias":"Create alias","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.title":"Publish new version from $LATEST","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.text":"Publishing a new version saves a snapshot of the code and the configuration of the $LATEST version. You need to deploy code changes in $LATEST before you can create a new version. Any triggers you added to the function are not saved to the new version. You can't change the new version's code. Choose Publish to confirm.","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.button.submit":"Publish","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.alert.success":"Successfully created version {version} for function {functionName}.","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.alert.notPublished":"No changes were made to $LATEST since publishing version {currentVersion}, so no version was published.","functionDetail.qualifiers.modal.publish.alert.failure":"An error occurred publishing a version: {err}","resourcePolicy.tableHeader":"Resource-based policy statements","resourcePolicy.buttons.delete":"Delete","resourcePolicy.buttons.add":"Add permissions","resourcePolicy.sid":"Statement ID","resourcePolicy.principal":"Principal","resourcePolicy.condition":"Conditions","resourcePolicy.conditions.ariaLabel":"Resource policy conditions","resourcePolicy.noConditions":"None","resourcePolicy.action":"Action","resourcePolicy.principalOrgId":"Principal Org ID","editResourcePolicy.header":"Edit resource-based policy","editResourcePolicyCreate.header":"Add permissions","editResourcePolicy.section.resourcePolicy.header":"Edit policy statement","editResourcePolicy.action.field.label":"Action","editResourcePolicy.action.placeholder":"Choose an action","editResourcePolicy.action.field.description":"Choose an action to allow.","editResourcePolicy.service.field.label":"Service","editResourcePolicy.tiles.account.label":"AWS account","editResourcePolicy.tiles.account.description":"Grant permissions to another AWS account, user, or role.","editResourcePolicy.tiles.service.label":"AWS service","editResourcePolicy.tiles.service.description":"Grant permissions to another AWS service.","functionDesigner.tab.permissions.resourcePolicy.jsonPolicy":"You created this statement using the JSON policy editor. Use the editor to view the statement and make changes.","modal.policy.delete.title":"Delete statement","modal.policy.delete.warning":"Deleting a policy statement permanently removes it from the resource policy. Any sources using these permissions might stop working as expected.","modal.policy.delete.expandableTitle":"View statement details","modal.policy.details.title":"Policy statement details","editResourcePolicy.service.field.description":"The AWS service to grant permissions to.","editResourcePolicy.sourceAccount.field.description":"The AWS account ID of the account that owns the specified resource. <learn-more> </learn-more>","editResourcePolicy.principal.field.description":"The service principal for this AWS service. <learn-more> </learn-more>","editResourcePolicy.functionUrl.action.nonEmpty":"This field is required. For more information, see <docs-link>Security and auth model for Lambda function URLs</docs-link>.","editResourcePolicy.principalOrgID.expandableSection.header":"Principal organization ID - <i>optional</i>","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyAlert.button":"Use JSON editor","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyTable.copyPolicy.button":"Copy policy","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyAlert.header":"JSON policy editor available","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyAlert.body":"Instead of adding individual permissions, create or edit a full resource-based policy for your function using the JSON editor. Creating a full policy gives you more flexibility to define the resources that can access your function. <learn-more>Learn more</learn-more>.","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyTable.simplePolicy.button":"Add individual permissions","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyTable.simplePolicyAlert.header":"Switch to simple policy editor","resourcePolicy.fullResourcePolicyTable.simplePolicyAlert.body":"Add permissions to your function individually instead of creating a full JSON policy. Adding permissions individually gives you less flexibility to define the resources that can access your function. <learn-more>Learn more</learn-more>.","editPolicyJson.header":"Edit resource-based policy","editPolicyJsonCreate.header":"Edit resource-based policy","editPolicyJson.blockPublicAccess.header":"Public access settings","editPolicyJson.editor.header":"Policy","blockPublicAccess.allowPublicPolicy.description":"Lambda will allow the creation of resource-based policies that grant public access to this function.","blockPublicAccess.allowPublicPolicy.header":"Allow public policies","blockPublicAccess.allowPublicResourceAccess.description":"Lambda will allow function URL endpoints for this function to be publicly accessible.","blockPublicAccess.allowPublicResourceAccess.header":"Allow public access to Function URLs","blockPublicAccess.description":"Manage public access permissions for your function.","blockPublicAccess.header":"Public access settings","blockPublicAccess.publicPolicy":"Resource-based policies","blockPublicAccess.publicResource":"Public resource access","blockPublicAccess.accessDenied.message":"Your AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role doesn't have permission to use lambda:{api}.","blockPublicAccess.alert.errorMessage":"There was an error calling lambda:GetPublicAccessBlockConfig.","editBlockPublicAccess.allow":"Allow public resource access","editBlockPublicAccess.block":"Block public resource access","editBlockPublicPolicy.allow":"Allow public policies","editBlockPublicPolicy.block":"Block public policies","editBlockPublicAccess.header":"Edit public access settings","editBlockPublicAccess.restrictPublicResource.field.label":"Public resource access","editBlockPublicAccess.restrictPublicResource.field.description":"Select 'Allow public resource access' to allow public access to Lambda resources with public policies.","editBlockPublicAccess.publicPolicy.field.label":"Resource-based policies","editBlockPublicAccess.publicPolicy.field.description":"Select 'Allow public policies' to allow the creation of resource-based policies that grant public access to your function.","trigger.create.title":"Add trigger","trigger.create.success":"The trigger {trigger} was successfully added to function {functionName}.","trigger.create.error":"An error occurred when creating the trigger: {error}","trigger.submitValidationError":"Please correct the errors above.","addRelation.permissions.modal.header":"Missing permissions","addRelation.permissions.modal.description":"Your Lambda function's execution role is missing required permissions. Do you want to automatically generate and attach them?","addRelation.permissions.modal.infoAlertContent":"Without these permissions, the operation may fail, or the Lambda function may not be able to consume messages from the source.","addRelation.permissions.modal.executionRole":"Execution role","addRelation.permissions.modal.skip":"Skip","addRelation.permissions.modal.generate":"Generate permissions","addRelation.permissions.modal.createStatus":"New policy will be generated","addRelation.permissions.modal.updateStatusSuffix":"will be updated","addRelation.permissions.modal.mskBasicPermissions":"MSK cluster permissions","addRelation.permissions.modal.learnMore":"Learn more","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.updateFailed.header":"Failed to update policy for {permissionType}","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.updateFailed.content":"could not be updated:","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.createFailed.header":"Failed to create policy for {permissionType}","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.createSuccess.header":"Successfully created policy for {permissionType}","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.createSuccess.content":"was successfully created and attached to your role.","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.updateSuccess.header":"Successfully updated policy for {permissionType}","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.updateSuccess.content":"was successfully updated.","addRelation.permissions.flashbar.generationFailed.header":"Permission generation failed","modal.blockPublicPolicy.save.alert.description":"We recommend that you don't allow public access to