 to write to the same bucket that invokes it. To ensure that your function does not invoke itself in a loop, use separate buckets for input and output. <learn-more />","header":"Potential recursive invocation"}},"deleteModal":{"confirmationMessage":"To confirm deletion, type \\"{{confirmationText}}\\" in the field.","content":{"alias":"Deleting this alias permanently removes only the alias, not the underlying version code and configuration. The logs and role aren\'t deleted. Are you sure you want to delete this alias?","durableFunction":"This function will enter \\"Deleting\\" status until all executions complete. The function code will be permanently removed, but logs, roles, test event schemas, and triggers are retained in your account.","function":"Deleting a function permanently removes the function code. The related logs, roles, test event schemas, and triggers are retained in your account.","hasInflightDurableExecutions":"This function has running executions that must complete before deletion.","version":"Deleting this version permanently removes the associated code and configuration. The logs and role aren\'t deleted. Are you sure you want to delete this version?"},"header":{"alias":"Delete alias {{qualifier}} from function {{functionName}}","function":"Delete function {{functionName}}","version":"Delete version {{qualifier}} from function {{functionName}}"}},"flashbar":{"action":{"activate":{"text":"Set scaling"},"cancelStateTransition":{"text":"Cancel"},"restore":{"text":"Restore"}},"createFailure":"Failed to create the function \\"{{functionName}}\\": {{message}}","createSuccess":"Successfully created the function \\"{{functionName}}\\". You can now change its code and configuration. To invoke your function with a test event, choose \\"Test\\".","createVersionFailure":"Couldn\'t create version {{qualifier}} of function \\"{{functionName}}\\": {{message}}","createVersionSuccess":"Successfully created version {{qualifier}} of function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","creating":"Creating the function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","creatingVersion":"Creating version {{qualifier}} of function \\"{{functionName}}\\". This might take a few minutes.","customBootstrapCreateSuccess":"Successfully created the function \\"{{functionName}}\\". Next, <3>add a layer</3> that contains your bootstrap and implement its handler. A sample bootstrap and handler have been provided for your reference. <5>Learn more</5>","deleteSuccess":{"alias":"Alias {{qualifier}} was successfully deleted from Lambda function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","function":"Your Lambda function \\"{{functionName}}\\" was successfully deleted.","version":"Version {{qualifier}} was successfully deleted from Lambda function \\"{{functionName}}\\"."},"deleting":"Your Lambda function \\"{{functionName}}\\" is being deleted. The function will remain available in read-only mode until all in-progress executions complete.","functionUpdate":{"content":"Changes to your function will update the runtime version.","header":"Runtime version locked until next function update."},"idle":"The function \\"{{functionName}}\\" is idle. To reactivate your function, choose \\"Restore\\".","latestPublished":{"action":{"text":"Publish"},"content":"Your function code or configuration has unpublished changes. The current test will use the latest published version. Publish your changes to test the updated version.","header":"Function has unpublished changes"},"restoreFailure":"Failed to restore the function \\"{{functionName}}\\": {{message}}","restoreSuccess":"Successfully restored the function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","restoring":"Restoring the function \\"{{functionName}}\\". This might take a few minutes.","throttled":{"action":{"text":"Edit concurrency"},"content":"Your function cannot be invoked while the reserved concurrency is zero.","header":"Function is throttled"},"updateFailure":"Failed to update the function \\"{{functionName}}\\": {{message}}","updateSuccess":"Successfully updated the function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","updateVersionFailure":"Failed to publish changes: {{message}}","updateVersionSuccess":"Successfully updated version {{qualifier}} for function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","updating":"Updating the function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","updatingVersion":"Updating version {{qualifier}} for function \\"{{functionName}}\\".","versionDeactivated":"Version {{qualifier}} is deactivated. To reactivate your function, choose \\"Set scaling\\" to set non-zero execution environment values.","versionDeactivating":"Deactivating version {{qualifier}}."},"header":{"action":{"throttle":{"text":"Throttle"}}},"qualifierSelector":{"filteringPlaceholder":"Search aliases and versions","loadingText":"Loading aliases and versions","options":{"alias":{"label":"Alias: {{name}}"},"aliases":{"label":"Aliases"},"function":{"label":"Function: {{functionName}}"},"version":{"label":"Version: {{version}}"},"versions":{"label":"Versions"}}},"throttleModal":{"action":{"throttle":{"text":"Confirm"}},"content":{"hasProvisionedConcurrency":"You can\'t throttle a function with provisioned concurrency that is configured on a version or alias. Remove all provisioned concurrency configurations before throttling.","safeToThrottle":"This action will set the reserved concurrency for <1>{{functionName}}</1> to zero, which will throttle all future invocations of this function. Please only use this in case of emergencies. For more information on what to do after you use this safeguard, read the <3>Managing Concurrency</3> documentation. If you would like to proceed, click Confirm, else click Cancel."},"header":"Throttle your function"}},"learnMore":"Learn more","listStateMachines":{"header":{"title":"Step Functions state machines"},"info":{"blurb":"AWS Step Functions is an orchestration service that lets you connect your Lambda functions into serverless workflows, called <i>state machines</i>. Build long-running workflows for IT automation and human-approval use cases, or create high-volume short-duration workflows for streaming data processing and ingestion. <learn-more />","branching":{"header":"Branching","text":"Design your workflow to choose different branches based on Lambda function output."},"chaining":{"header":"Chaining","text":"Connect functions into a series of steps, with the output of one step providing the input to the next step."},"header":"Build serverless workflows with state machines","new":{"buttonText":"Get started","header":"New to Step Functions?","text":"Get started in minutes with a sample Lambda workflow."},"parallelism":{"header":"Parallelism","text":"Run functions in parallel, or use dynamic parallelism to invoke a function for every member of any array."},"retry":{"header":"Catch and retry","text":"Handle errors using sophisticated catch-and-retry functionality."}}},"loading":"Loading","navigation":{"canvas":{"popover":{"content":"Explore all of Lambda\'s capabilities in a single dynamic interface.","header":"Introducing the canvas"}},"microvms":{"popover":{"content":"Use Lambda MicroVMs to build AI coding assistants, interactive data analytics platforms, and secure code execution environments.","header":"Introducing MicroVMs"}},"section":{"additionalResources":{"runtimes":{"popover":{"content":"Run Lambda functions in your preferred language or environment, beyond the AWS-provided managed runtimes.","header":"Introducing customer-managed runtimes"}}},"documentation":"Documentation","eventFunctionResources":{"label":"Event Function resources"},"relatedAwsResources":"Related AWS resources","serverlessWorkshops":{"label":"Serverless workshops"},"webFunctions":{"popover":{"content":"Build web applications and APIs that listen on a port, with built-in endpoints and active-duration billing.","header":"Introducing Web Functions"}}}},"newAndOptional":"new, optional","newFeature":"new","newFeature_sidebar":"New","no":"No","noMatch":{"action":{"text":"Clear filter"},"title":"No matches"},"optional":"optional","pageName":{"addRdsDatabase":"Connect to RDS database","addRdsDatabaseProxy":"Add database proxy","addRelation":"Add triggers","appGenerator":"App builder","begin":"AWS Lambda","canvas":"Canvas","configureApplication":"Review, configure and deploy","connectMicroVM":"Connect to :vmId","createApplicationConfigure":"Configure your application","createApplicationDiscover":"Create application","createCapacityProvider":"Create capacity provider","createCodeSigningConfiguration":"Create code signing configuration","createFunction":"Create function","createLayer":"Create layer","createLayerVersion":"Create version","createMicroVMImage":"Create MicroVM Image","createNetworkConnector":"Create network connector","createRuntime":"Create runtime","createRuntimeAlias":"Create alias","createRuntimeVersion":"Create version","createWebFunction":"Create Web Function","discover":"Dashboard","editAlias":"Edit alias","editAliasCreate":"Create alias","editAsync":"Edit asynchronous configuration","editBasicSettings":"Edit basic settings","editBlockPublicAccess":"Edit public access settings","editCapacityProvider":"Edit capacity provider configuration","editCapacityProviderLoggingConfiguration":"Edit capacity provider logging configuration","editCapacityProviderScaling":"Edit function scaling","editCapacityProviderTagPropagation":"Manage tags for propagation","editCapacityProviderTags":"Manage tags","editCodeSigning":"Edit code signing","editCodeSigningConfiguration":"Edit code signing configuration","editCodeSigningConfigurationTags":"Manage tags","editConcurrency":"Edit concurrency","editDestination":"Edit destination","editDestinationCreate":"Add destination","editDistributedMapRun":"Edit concurrency and failure tolerance","editDurableConfiguration":"Edit durable configuration settings","editEnvironmentVariables":"Edit environment variables","editEventSourceMappingTags":"Manage tags","editFileSystem":"Edit file system","editFileSystemCreate":"Add file system","editFunctionUrl":"Configure Function URL","editImageConfiguration":"Edit image configuration","editImageSettings":"Select image","editLayers":"Edit layers","editLayerVersionFunctions":"Edit layer version for functions","editLoggingConfiguration":"Edit logging configuration","editMicroVMImage":"Edit :imageName","editMonitoringTools":"Edit monitoring tools","editNetworkConnector":"Edit network connector","editPolicyJson":"Edit resource-based policy","editPolicyJsonCreate":"Edit resource-based policy","editProvisionedConcurrency":"Configure provisioned concurrency","editProvisionedConcurrencyCreate":"Configure provisioned concurrency","editRecursionConfig":"Edit recursive loop detection","editRelation":"Edit trigger","editResourcePolicy":"Edit resource-based policy","editResourcePolicyCreate":"Add permissions","editRuntimeAlias":"Update alias","editRuntimeDetails":"Edit basic information","editRuntimePermissions":"Edit runtime permissions","editRuntimePolicy":"Edit runtime management configuration","editRuntimeSettings":"Edit runtime settings","editRuntimeTags":"Edit tags","editTags":"Manage tags","editVpc":"Edit VPC","editWebFunctionPermissions":"Edit permissions","extensions":"Extensions","functionDesignerAlias":"Alias: :alias","functionDesignerVersion":"Version: :version","listApplications":"Applications","listCapacityProviders":"Capacity providers","listCodeSigningConfigurations":"Code signing configurations","listEventFunctions":"Event Functions","listEventSourceMappings":"Event source mappings","listLayers":"Layers","listMicroVMImages":"MicroVM Images","listMicroVMs":"MicroVMs","listNetworkConnectors":"Network connectors","listReplicas":"Replicas","listRuntimes":"Runtimes","listStateMachines":"Step Functions state machines","listWebFunctions":"Web Functions","manageRuntimeAliasLifecycle":"Manage alias lifecycle","manageRuntimeLifecycle":"Manage runtime lifecycle","networkConnectorVersion":"Version: {{version}}","publishLayerVersion":"Publish layer version","runMicroVM":"Run MicroVM","viewCapacityProvider":":capacityProviderName"},"playground":{"header":"How it works","next":"Next: {{step}}","run":"Run","step":{"code":{"customRuntime":"Customer-managed runtime","editor":"Lambda sample code","testing":"Running...","text":"Above is a simple Lambda function. Click \\"Run\\" to see function output before going to the next step.","title":"Just write the code"},"events":{"text":"Once you create Lambda functions, you can configure them to respond to events from a variety of sources. Try sending a mobile notification, streaming data to Lambda, or placing a photo in an S3 bucket.","title":"Lambda responds to events"},"scale":{"cost":"Cost: <1>{{cost}}</1> *","disclaimer":"* Your first 1 million requests or 400,000 GB-seconds of compute per month are free. Costs in this demo are based on a 128 MB function with a 1 second invocation duration.","invocations":"Invocations: <1>{{invocations}}</1>","text":"Lambda scales up and down automatically to handle your workloads, and you don\'t pay anything when your code isn\'t running.","title":"Scale seamlessly"}},"visualization":{"backends":"Mobile / IoT backends","data":"Data processing","streams":"Streaming analytics"}},"previous":"Previous","productName":"Lambda","refresh":"Refresh","refreshComplete":"Refresh complete","refreshing":"Refreshing","relationBuilder":{"core":{"enteredTextLabel":"Use: \\"{{value}}\\""},"sourceNodeFilteringPlaceholder":"Search trigger sources","sourceNodeSelectPlaceholder":"Select a source","submitValidationError":"Please correct the errors above.","targetNodeFilteringPlaceholder":"Search trigger targets","targetNodeSelectPlaceholder":"Select a target"},"relationList":{"detailsAriaLabel":"Details for {{name}}.","detailsValueFalse":"No","detailsValueNone":"None","detailsValueTrue":"Yes","fixModalRunButtonText":"Fix errors","modalStopButtonText":"Stop","tableActionsFixText":"Fix errors"},"remove":"Remove","resourceTable":{"emptyText":"There is no data to display.","failed":"Failed to fetch","filteringPlaceholder":"Search by attributes or search by keyword","filteringPropertiesGroupValuesLabel":"{{propertyLabel}} values","lastFetchedText":"Last fetched <1></1>","preferencesPageSizeOptionLabel":"{{value}} resources","tags":{"properties":"Tags","values":"Tag values"}},"rolePermissions":{"field":{"addRolePermissions":{"label":"Add required permissions"}},"headerText":"Permissions"},"save":"Save","search":{"badge":{"application":"Application","tag":"Tagged"},"index":{"notConfiguredDescription":"To search for Lambda functions, you need to set up AWS Resource Explorer in your account. Resource Explorer indexes your AWS resources and enables cross-region search at no cost.","notConfiguredError":"AWS Resource Explorer is not initialized","setupButton":"Set up Resource Explorer"},"input":{"placeholder":"Search functions by name"},"keys":{"navigate":"to navigate","select":"to select"},"mode":{"help":"Display this help","module":"Search for a module","resource":"Search for a resource"},"status":{"error":"Failed to search","info":"Type to search for a function","loading":"Searching...","success":"Viewing {{visible}} of {{total}} results"}},"softDelete":{"deletingInDays_one":"Deleting in {{count}} day","deletingInDays_many":"Deleting in {{count}} days","deletingInDays_other":"Deleting in {{count}} days","deletionPeriodPopover":"Scheduled for permanent deletion on","deletionPeriodRemaining_one":"{{count}} day","deletionPeriodRemaining_many":"{{count}} days","deletionPeriodRemaining_other":"{{count}} days","pendingDeletion":"Pending deletion"},"stop":"Stop","table":{"allItemsSelectionLabel":"Select all items"},"tagEditorContainer":{"header":{"description":"A tag is a label that you assign to an AWS resource. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value. You can use tags to search and filter your resources, track your AWS costs, and enforce attribute-based access control.","title":"Tags"}},"tagsTable":{"column":{"header":{"key":"Key","value":"Value"}},"empty":{"title":"No tags"},"filteringPlaceholder":"Search for tags","header":{"action":{"manage":{"text":"Manage tags"}}},"title":"Tags"},"targeting":{"recommendedForYou":{"alert":{"failedToLoad":{"content":"Recommendations could not be loaded. Refresh the page to try again."}},"header":{"title":"Recommended for you"}}},"tutorial":{"feedbackMessage":"Guided Workflow Feedback"},"tutorials":{"completionScreenTitle":"Congratulations! You completed the tutorial.","dismissTutorialButtonText":"Dismiss tutorial","feedbackLinkText":"Feedback","finishButtonText":"Finish","functionUrl":{"completedScreenDescription":"<0>Now you know how to create a simple webapp: an HTTP endpoint using a Lambda function with a public Function URL. When you\'re done with the resources that you created in this tutorial, delete them to avoid unnecessary charges to your account.</0><1><0>To delete the Function URL</0><1><0>Choose the <1>Configuration tab</1>, and then choose <3>Function URL</3>.</0><1>Choose <1>Delete</1>.</1><2>In the dialog box, follow the prompts to delete the Function URL.</2></1></1><2><0>To delete the function</0><1><0>Choose <1>Actions</1>, and then choose <3>Delete function</3>.</0><1>In the dialog box, choose <1>Delete</1>.</1></1></2><3>Next, we recommend exploring other common ways to deploy Lambda functions. For example, by using .zip file archives and container images. For more information, see <1>Deploying Lambda functions</1>.</3>","description":"<0>In this tutorial you will learn how to:</0><1><0>Build a simple web app, consisting of a Lambda function with a function URL that outputs a webpage</0><1>Invoke your function through its function URL</1></1>","task1":{"step1":{"content":"Choose <1>Use a blueprint</1>. Blueprints are pre-packaged code templates that provide skeleton code for a variety of Lambda use cases. <3></3>","title":"Choose \\"Use a blueprint\\""},"step2":{"content":"<0>For <1>Blueprint name</1>, choose <3>Getting started with Lambda HTTP</3>. This blueprint contains an index.html file, along with function code that outputs this HTML. You will review this code after creating the function.</0><1>This blueprint also sets up a function URL. A Function URL is a dedicated HTTP endpoint that you can visit to invoke your lambda function and view the rendered HTML output.</1>","title":"Choose the blueprint"},"step3":{"content":"Enter <1>Function name</1>, for example <3>http-function-url-tutorial</3>.","title":"Name your function"},"step4":{"blockPublicAccess":{"title":"Allow public access","warning":"You\'re creating a publicly accessible HTTP endpoint, so anyone with your URL can access it. To create this endpoint, make sure your function\'s settings are configured to allow public access."},"content":"At the end of the tutorial, you can delete the Function URL to avoid unneccessary charges to your account. For more information, see <1>Security and auth model for Lambda function URLs</1> and <3>Lambda Pricing</3>.","title":"Acknowledge public Function URL statement","warning":"You\'re creating a public HTTP endpoint, so anyone on the internet can access it using your Function URL. Before you proceed, read and acknowledge this Function URL statement."},"step5":{"content":"Choose <1>Create function</1>. This deploys the code.","title":"Complete function creation"},"title":"Create the function"},"task2":{"step1":{"content":"<0>Before you invoke the function, review the code that you deployed in the previous step. Choose the <1>Code</1> tab to view the built-in code editor.</0><1>The <1>index.mjs</1> file contains your function code. The code returns an HTTP response with a body that contains the contents of the <3>index.html</3> file. You can also open the index.html file in the code editor to view its contents.</1>","title":"Review the function code"},"step2":{"content":"<0>Each time that a user visits your Function URL endpoint, they invoke your Lambda function. To invoke your function, open the Function URL endpoint in a browser. You should see the rendered HTML output, which contains links to additional Lambda tutorials that you can try.</0><1>FURLs are only one way to invoke your functions. You can invoke Lambda functions directly via the console or Lambda API. You can also configure other AWS services to invoke your functions in response to events. <1></1></1>","title":"Invoke your Function URL"},"title":"Invoke the function"},"title":"Create a simple web app"},"labelDismissAnnotation":"Dismiss annotation","labelExitTutorial":"Dismiss tutorial","labelHotspot":"Annotation for step {{stepIndex}} of {{totalStepCount}}","labelLearnMoreExternalIcon":"Opens in a new tab","labelLearnMoreLink":"Learn more about lambda invocations (opens new tab)","labelsTaskStatusInProgress":"In progress","labelsTaskStatusPending":"Pending","labelsTaskStatusSuccess":"Complete","labelTotalSteps":"Total steps: {{totalStepCount}}","labelTutorialListDownloadLink":"Download PDF version of this tutorial","learnMoreLinkText":"Learn more","loadingText":"Loading","nextButtonText":"Next","previousButtonText":"Previous","restartTutorialButtonText":"Restart tutorial","startTutorialButtonText":"Start tutorial","stepCounterText":"Step {{stepIndex}} of {{totalStepCount}}","stepTitle":"Step {{stepIndex}}: {{stepTitle}}","taskTitle":"Task {{taskIndex}}: {{taskTitle}}","tutorialCompletedText":"Tutorial completed","tutorialListDescription":"Learn how to implement common use cases in AWS Lambda.","tutorialListDownloadLinkText":"Download PDF version","tutorialListTitle":"Choose a tutorial","webFunctionApp":{"completedScreenDescription":"<0>Now you know how to create a simple web app: a Lambda Web Function with a public endpoint that serves a webpage. When you\'re done with the resources that you created in this tutorial, delete them to avoid incurring charges to your account.</0><1><0>To delete the Web Function</0><1><0>Open the Web Function\'s detail page, then choose <1>Delete</1>.</0><1>In the dialog box, follow the prompts to delete the Web Function.</1></1></1><2>Next, we recommend exploring how to deploy new revisions and route traffic between them.</2>","description":"<0>In this tutorial you will learn how to:</0><1><0>Build a simple web app using a Lambda Web Function that returns an HTML webpage</0><1>Invoke your Web Function through its endpoint URL</1></1>","task1":{"step1":{"content":"Enter a <1>Function name</1>, for example <3>my-web-app</3>.","title":"Name your Web Function"},"step2":{"content":"<0>Keep <1>Hello world</1> selected as the code source. This sample serves a simple webpage and is a good starting point for a web app.</0><1>You can expand the code preview to review the files that will be deployed.</1>","title":"Choose your code source and review the sample code"},"step3":{"content":"<0>Under <1>Endpoint configuration</1>, enter an <3>Endpoint name</3>, for example <5>default</5>.</0><1>Keep the default <1>Home-Region</1> endpoint type.</1>","title":"Name your endpoint"},"step4":{"content":"For <1>Authentication type</1>, choose <3>Application-managed authentication</3>. Your function code controls access, so the endpoint is publicly reachable without IAM request signing.","title":"Choose the authentication type"},"step5":{"content":"Choose <1>Create Web Function</1>. This deploys your code as a new revision and provisions the endpoint.","title":"Create the Web Function"},"title":"Create the Web Function"},"task2":{"step1":{"content":"<0>After your Web Function becomes <1>Active</1>, open its endpoint URL to invoke the function and view the rendered webpage.</0>","title":"Open your endpoint URL"},"title":"Invoke your Web Function"},"title":"Create a simple web app"}},"validation":{"arnRegex":"Invalid ARN.","invalidType":"This field must be of \\"{{expected}}\\" type.","jsonschema":{"divisibleBy":"This field must be of the \\"integer\\" type.","enum":"Your input is invalid.","maximum":"The maximum allowed value for this field is %{expected}.","maxItems":"The maximum allowed number of items for this field is %{expected}.","maxLength":"This field is too long. The maximum length is %{expected} characters.","minimum":"The minimum allowed value for this field is %{expected}.","minItems":"The minimum allowed number of items for this field is %{expected}.","minLength":"This field is too short. The minimum length is %{expected} characters.","nonEmpty":"This field is required.","pattern":"Invalid input.","required":"This field is required.","type":"This field must be of \\"%{expected}\\" type.","uniqueItems":"This field must not contain duplicate items.","uniqueItemsProperty":"This field must not contain duplicate items."},"minMax":"Minimum value {{minimum}} must be less than or equal to maximum value {{maximum}}.","regex":"Invalid input.","required":"This field is required.","s3UrlRegex":"This URL must be a valid Amazon S3 URL — for example, https://s3.{{apiDomain}}/bucket/path or s3://bucket/path.","tooBig":{"number":"This value is too large. The maximum value is {{maximum}}.","other":"This field is too long. The maximum length is {{maximum}} characters."},"tooSmall":{"number":"This value is too small. The minimum value is {{minimum}}.","other":"This field is too short. The minimum length is {{minimum}} characters."},"uniqueItemsBy":"This field must not contain duplicate items.","zipUpload":{"maxSize":"The selected file is too large. The maximum size is {{maxSize}}.","required":"You have chosen to upload a file but have not selected a file yet."}},"viewApplication":{"codeTools":{"blurb":"Use AWS tools to build and test your application locally before deploying. The AWS SAM CLI, AWS Cloud9, and the AWS Toolkit work together to enable you to test changes to your application\'s code and supporting resources before pushing changes to your source repository. You can also use the AWS Toolkit to troubleshoot issues with step-through debugging.","header":"Developer tools","jetbrains":{"description":"Develop, compile, and test your application code in IntelliJ or PyCharm."},"samcli":{"description":"Build, test, and debug application code locally in a Docker container that emulates the Lambda execution environment."},"visualstudio":{"description":"Develop, compile, and test your application code in Visual Studio."},"vscode":{"description":"Develop, compile, and test your application code in Visual Studio Code."}},"deploymentTools":{"blurb":"You can use the following tools to automate deployment of your serverless applications. <learn-more />","codebuild":{"description":"Compile, test, and package function code."},"codedeploy":{"description":"Deploy changes to your function code gradually and safely. AWS CodeDeploy manages function aliases to perform a rolling deployment that can be rolled back automatically."},"codepipeline":{"description":"Combine AWS CodeBuild and AWS CodeDeploy into a continuous delivery pipeline for your serverless application."},"header":"Set up a deployment pipeline"},"error":{"failedStackEvent":"Failed to execute changes on <1>{{resource}}</1> because: {{reason}}"},"flashbar":{"createSuccess":"Application created","creating":{"header":"Creating application resources. This takes a few minutes.","step1":"Step 1 of 4 - Creating repository","step2":"Step 2 of 4 - Creating pipeline","step3":"Step 3 of 4 - Building and packaging application","step4":"Step 4 of 4 - Creating application stack"},"error":"Error creating application"},"gettingStarted":{"basic":{"blurb":"Welcome to your new application view. From here, you can view the resources that make up your application, and monitor performance, errors, and traffic metrics. <learn-more />","codeTools":{"header":"Set up your development environment","text":"You can use the following tools and services to build, test, and deploy your applications."},"partners":"AWS Lambda Partners provide services and tools that you can use with your Lambda functions. <1>View all the current AWS Lambda Partners</1>"},"header":"Getting started","lambdaApplication":{"infrastructure":{"header":"Continuous delivery infrastructure","text":"When you commit changes to the master branch and push them to AWS CodeCommit or GitHub, the application\'s pipeline builds, packages, and deploys your changes automatically. For a list of the supporting resources that enable continuous delivery for your application, see below. Under <1>Deployments</1>, you can find details about the pipeline that connects source, build, and deployment resources."},"sam":{"header":"Add AWS resources and service permissions","text":"To add AWS resources and triggers to your application, define them in the AWS SAM template that\'s included with the application\'s source code. The template also defines the execution role for the application\'s function or functions. You can extend this role to access more services and resources from your code. Execution roles also provide access to Lambda event source mappings that read from services such as Amazon SQS. <learn-more />"},"welcome":{"header":"Your serverless application","text":"The application repository contains the function code, template, and build configuration that define your application. For an overview of its structure and steps to get started, view the <1>README</1>. The <3>Code</3> tab shows information about the source repository and tools for local development and testing. To see metrics from your application and analyze logs, choose <5>Monitoring</5>."}},"youtube":{"title":"YouTube video player: Serverless Applications, Automated Deployments, and the AWS Lambda Console"}},"tab":{"code":{"label":"Code"},"deployments":{"label":"Deployments"},"monitoring":{"label":"Monitoring"},"overview":{"label":"Overview"}}},"viewCapacityProvider":{"create":"Create function","deleteModal":{"confirmationMessage":"To confirm deletion, type \\"{{confirmationText}}\\" in the field.","content":{"hasFunctions":"This capacity provider is in use by one or more functions and can\'t be deleted. For a list of the functions using this capacity provider, see the capacity provider\'s details page.","safeToDelete":"Delete {{capacityProviderName}} permanently? This action can\'t be undone.","warning":"Proceeding with this action will delete the capacity provider and will remove its scaling and capacity management settings."},"header":"Delete capacity provider {{capacityProviderName}}"},"flashbar":{"deleteSuccess":"Capacity provider {{capacityProviderName}} was successfully deleted.","state":{"Deleting":{"content":"Deleting capacity provider {{capacityProviderName}}."},"Failed":{"button":"Restore","content":"Previous action failed for capacity provider {{capacityProviderName}}."},"Pending":{"content":"Updating capacity provider {{capacityProviderName}}."}}},"tab":{"additionalConfiguration":"Additional configuration","functions":"Function versions","monitoring":"Monitor","tags":"Tags"}},"viewCodeSigningConfiguration":{"deleteModal":{"content":{"hasFunctions":"The code signing configuration can\'t be deleted while it\'s in use by one or more functions. For a list of functions using this configuration, see the configuration\'s detail page.","safeToDelete":"The code signing configuration can be safely deleted."},"header":"Delete code signing configuration {{codeSigningConfigurationId}}"},"flashbar":{"deleteSuccess":"Successfully deleted the code signing configuration {{codeSigningConfigurationId}}"},"tab":{"functions":{"label":"Functions using this configuration"},"tags":{"label":"Tags"}}},"viewEventSourceMapping":{"deleteModal":{"content":"Deleting an event source mapping permanently removes it from Lambda. The event source itself will not be deleted.","header":"Delete event source mapping {{uuid}}"},"flashbar":{"deleteSuccess":"Successfully deleted the event source mapping {{uuid}}"},"tab":{"details":{"label":"Details"},"monitor":{"label":"Monitor"},"tags":{"label":"Tags"}}},"viewLayer":{"deleteModal":{"content":"Deleting this layer version will permanently remove the associated code and configuration. Invocations of functions using the version will continue working. Are you sure you want to delete this Lambda layer version?","header":"Delete {{layerName}} version: {{version}}"},"flashbar":{"deleteSuccess":"The version {{version}} of your Lambda layer \\"{{layerName}}\\" was successfully deleted."},"header":{"action":{"createVersion":{"text":"Create version"},"download":{"text":"Download"}}},"tab":{"functions":{"label":"Functions using this version"},"versions":{"label":"Versions"}}},"viewNetworkConnector":{"deleteModal":{"confirmationMessage":"To confirm deletion, type \\"{{confirmationText}}\\" in the field.","content":"Permanently delete network connector {{networkConnectorName}}? Any Lambda compute resources using this connector will lose VPC connectivity. This action cannot be undone.","header":"Delete network connector {{networkConnectorName}}","warning":"Deleting this network connector will interrupt active VPC connectivity. Make sure no Lambda compute resources are actively using this connector before proceeding."},"flashbar":{"deleteSuccess":"Network connector {{networkConnectorName}} was successfully deleted."}},"viewParentLayer":{"deleteLayer":"Delete layer","deleteModal":{"confirmationMessage":"To confirm deletion, type \\"{{confirmationText}}\\" in the field.","content":{"confirm":"This cannot be undone. Are you sure you want to delete the layer \\"{{layerName}}\\"?","warning":"Deleting this layer will permanently delete all of its layer versions, including code and configuration. Functions already using a version of this layer will continue to run, but you will not be able to add this layer to a function, update a function that still references it, or publish a new function version with the layer attached."},"flashbar":{"success":"Deletion of layer \\"{{layerName}}\\" started. This removes all versions of the layer and may take a few moments to complete."},"header":"Delete layer {{layerName}}?"},"tab":{"functions":{"label":"Functions using this layer"},"tags":{"label"